  "scope": "A final-request-only consuming transfer preserves original identity, domain, remaining Fuel and limits without a synthetic binding frame, callback, clone or dispatch. Initial/binding/accepted/terminal states refuse unchanged. Final restore validates policy ceilings before native admission and reuses SessionCore AwaitingFinal/AcceptedFinal and explicit final projection. The host validates original request correspondence, budget, current authority and nonterminal settlement. Local restoration revokes before retained identity/error/unused-hook cleanup on refusal or unwind; callback revocation wins. Reply cleanup inside native projection remains trusted and may precede the outer fence. Two hosts cover direct and captured-helper final calls, transfer before and after actual dispatch, every fuel cutoff, stale/invalid owned replies, revocation, cancellation and once-only final output. No production durable codec, crash settlement or complete graph recovery is claimed.",
